# Frontend git workflow (published SPA in Bedrock)

Layout:

- `web/frontend/src/` — Vite project ([ports-sacco-frontend](https://github.com/jkkenzie/ports-sacco-frontend); nested git). **This is the only place to edit React/SPA source.**
- `web/frontend/` — published SPA (`index.html`, `assets/`, …) tracked by Bedrock. **Never edit these files by hand.** They are generated by the build.

## Source changes (ports-sacco-frontend)

Edit under `web/frontend/src/` only (typically `web/frontend/src/src/`). Do not patch hashed bundles, `index.html`, or CSS in `web/frontend/assets/`.

```bash
cd web/frontend/src
# edit, commit/push to ports-sacco-frontend as usual
git add .
git commit -m "Describe source change"
git push origin main
```

## Publish into Bedrock (for server `git pull`)

Run the build from the Vite project after source changes (or when the user asks). It writes `dist/` then copies into `web/frontend/`.

```bash
cd web/frontend/src
npm run build          # vite → dist/ → publish up to web/frontend/
cd ../../..            # Bedrock root
git add web/frontend/index.html web/frontend/assets web/frontend/favicon.svg web/frontend/team-bg.png web/frontend/team-bg.svg
git commit -m "Update published SPA build"
git push origin main
```

Server: `git pull` only — no npm, no copy from `dist/`.
